Package: rbe
Title: Rule-Based Ensembles
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Max", "Kuhn", , "max@posit.co", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2402-136X")),
    person("Posit Software, PBC", role = c("cph", "fnd"),
           comment = c(ROR = "03wc8by49"))
  )
Description: Fit RuleFit models for regression and classification, as
    described by Friedman and Popescu (2008) <doi:10.1214/07-AOAS148>. A boosted
    tree ensemble creates a set of rules, and a regularized generalized
    linear model from 'glmnet' is fit to the original predictors and binary
    indicators for the rules. The rules can be made with 'xgboost' (Chen
    and Guestrin (2016) <doi:10.1145/2939672.2939785>), 'lightgbm' (Ke et
    al. (2017)
    <https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper/2017/hash/6449f44a102fde848669bdd9eb6b76fa-Abstract.html>),
    or 'catboost' (Prokhorenkova et al. (2018) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1706.09516>).
